  "query_preview": "..\nIssued 1136 PM CDT Thu Aug 27 2026\n\nSaturday through Thursday:\n\nA broad, but low amplitude upper ridge, will move into the \ncentral and srn USA this weekend and continue into next week.\nWell organized low to mid level warm, moist advection that will\nbring the ridge into the central USA, will affect srn WI Sat \nafternoon and night. PWATs will rise above 1.5 inches but mid \nlevel lapse rates will remain poor through Sat nt with only very\nlimited CAPE developing. Showers are still likely with some \nstorms Sat afternoon and night when the main tropospheric \nbaroclinic zone moves across the region. The mid level lapse\nrates will steepen on Sunday as the elevated mixed layer arrives\nbut the warming temps aloft will also contribute to capping.\nMUCAPE should rise above 1000 J/KG for Sun-Mon and some warm, \nmoist advection will continue on a swly low level jet into Mon.\nRain chances of 20-50 percent are forecast. \n\nA shortwave trough will then pass to the north Tue nt but drag a\nweak cold front through srn WI. 40 percent chances for showers\nand storms are forecast. Afterward an upper ridge will either\nbuild through the Great Plains or back nwd into the central USA\nand Upper MS River Valley. Overall a very warm and humid week\nis expected beginning on Sunday. \n\n\nGehring",
